  "helpTitle": "Help",
  "helpIntro": "Offline explanations of the main MusicArk workflows and what each section does.",
  "helpGettingStartedTitle": "Using MusicArk",
  "helpGettingStartedBody": "Choose a topic below. Help explains what each section is for, how similar states differ, and which actions can modify local files.",
  "helpGroupLibrary": "Library",
  "helpGroupAnalysis": "Collection analysis",
  "helpGroupRecovery": "Recovery and actions",
  "helpGroupApplication": "Application",
  "helpYandexTitle": "Yandex Music",
  "helpYandexBody": "Shows your cached and refreshed Yandex Music library: liked tracks, playlists and liked albums. It does not upload local files to Yandex Music.",
  "helpYandexSummary": "Provider library with liked tracks, playlists and explicitly liked albums.",
  "helpYandexDetails": "This section shows the cached and refreshed Yandex Music view: liked tracks, playlists and explicitly liked albums. Sign-in uses the existing Yandex Music session; MusicArk does not create a separate account. Refreshing the provider library does not rewrite local audio files or upload them back to Yandex Music.\n\nWhen to use it: when you need to inspect the desired collection state on the music-provider side.",
  "helpLocalTitle": "Local Library",
  "helpLocalBody": "Indexes configured local music folders. Scanning reads your audio files and updates the MusicArk index; it does not rewrite or delete the audio files.",
  "helpLocalSummary": "Index of configured music folders without hidden file mutation.",
  "helpLocalDetails": "Configured folders are indexed by MusicArk. A normal scan reads audio files and refreshes the local index; it does not rewrite or delete those files. Matching and Coverage use this index. Local Library artwork priority is embedded artwork, then already-cached Yandex artwork for a confirmed identity, then a placeholder.\n\nIf a file is missing from the view: confirm that it is inside a configured folder, run the scan again, and verify that its format is supported by the current read path.",
  "helpMatchingTitle": "Matching",
  "helpMatchingBody": "Connects a Yandex track identity with a local file using available evidence. Matching answers which track it is; Variant analysis separately checks whether the recording/version differs.",
  "helpMatchingSummary": "Determines which provider track corresponds to a local file.",
  "helpMatchingDetails": "Matching establishes identity: which music-provider track corresponds to a local file. It uses the available evidence and confidence, but a high similarity score alone is not a user-confirmed identity.\n\nImportant: Identity ≠ Metadata. Identity ≠ Variant. Similarity ≠ confirmed identity. An explicit provider identity is created only through an existing confirmation workflow, such as Apply + Bind in Metadata Editor.",
  "helpVariantTitle": "Track versions and censorship",
  "helpVariantSummary": "Checks the recording/version separately and stores ORIGINAL / CENSORED labels.",
  "helpVariantDetails": "The same track identity may exist as different recordings or versions. Variant analysis uses SAME, ALTERED, DIFFERENT_VERSION and UNCERTAIN states. DIFFERENT_VERSION does not automatically mean Missing.\n\nAccepting the current recording stores a separate user decision and does not turn the analyzer result into SAME. ORIGINAL / CENSORED are MusicArk application-level labels: they do not increase Matching confidence, modify Yandex Music data, or rewrite local audio metadata.",
  "helpMissingTitle": "Missing",
  "helpMissingBody": "Shows provider tracks that are not currently covered by an acceptable local file. A Different Version result is a separate review state and is not automatically equivalent to Missing.",
  "helpMissingSummary": "Provider tracks without acceptable local coverage.",
  "helpMissingDetails": "Missing means that a provider track currently has no acceptable local coverage. Missing ≠ Different Version: a differing recording remains a separate review state. A poor or unaccepted match must not become acceptable coverage automatically.\n\nFrom this section you can mark a track Wanted or Ignored, reset that decision, and explicitly start the existing Download workflow when it is available for the track.",
  "helpDownloadsTitle": "Downloads",
  "helpDownloadsBody": "Shows requested acquisitions and their status. Downloads are explicit tasks; this section does not silently rewrite existing local files.",
  "helpDownloadsSummary": "Queue of explicit tasks for acquiring a local track copy.",
  "helpDownloadsDetails": "Downloads shows explicitly created download tasks and their state. Main user-visible states are Queued, Downloading, Completed, Error, Needs review, Cancelled and Skipped. An existing local file is not silently overwritten. Removing a failed task removes the task record rather than the final audio file.\n\nAfter a successful acquisition, the collection state is determined by the existing indexing, Matching and Coverage flows rather than by the visual task status alone.",
  "helpSyncTitle": "Sync",
  "helpSyncBody": "Builds and applies a controlled plan for wanted missing tracks. Sync does not delete local-only files and does not automatically replace a Different Version recording.",
  "helpSyncSummary": "Controlled plan for restoring local coverage of the collection.",
  "helpSyncDetails": "Conceptually, Yandex Music describes the desired collection, Local Library describes the files actually present, and Sync builds a controlled plan to restore coverage. The planner calculates the plan first, and Apply requires explicit confirmation.\n\nNormal Sync is not a bidirectional filesystem mirror: it does not delete local-only files, move or rename existing audio, change existing metadata, automatically replace a Different Version recording, or mutate the Yandex Music collection.",
  "helpMetadataTitle": "Metadata Editor",
  "helpMetadataBody": "Explicitly edits supported metadata of one existing local file. Apply Metadata writes selected metadata but does not confirm identity. Apply + Bind writes metadata and explicitly binds the file to the selected provider identity.",
  "helpMetadataSummary": "The normal explicit-write workflow for an existing local audio file.",
  "helpMetadataDetails": "Metadata Editor can change an existing local file only after an explicit user action. Apply Metadata writes the selected fields, artwork and, when explicitly chosen, the filename, but it does not confirm identity. Apply + Bind performs the write and additionally creates a confirmed relation with the selected provider identity. Metadata ≠ Identity.\n\nFull safe writing is implemented for MP3/ID3; other audio formats remain read-only in Metadata Editor. A successful write is followed by single-file reindexing, SHA-256 refresh and a targeted Matching refresh.",
  "helpArtworkTitle": "Artwork and playback",
  "helpArtworkSummary": "Where artwork comes from and why playback cache is not Local Library content.",
  "helpArtworkDetails": "Local Library artwork priority is embedded artwork → already-cached provider artwork for a confirmed identity → placeholder. Local rows do not make a separate Yandex Music request per track.\n\nYandex Music tracks can be played inside MusicArk. The backend prepares or reuses a private local playback cache and gives Flutter only a local path. Playback-cache files are not indexed into Local Library and do not affect Matching or Coverage; protected provider media URLs and credentials are not passed to Flutter.",
  "helpSettingsTitle": "Settings",
  "helpSettingsSummary": "Theme and language apply immediately and are stored separately from the music database.",
  "helpSettingsDetails": "Theme supports System, Light and Dark. Language supports the system choice, Russian and English. Changes apply without restarting and are saved automatically. UI preferences are stored separately from the music SQLite database and do not contain provider credentials or collection contents.",
  "helpSafetyTitle": "Data safety",
  "helpSafetySummary": "Which workflows only analyze data and which one can actually modify a file.",
  "helpSafetyDetails": "A normal Scan reads files and updates the index. Matching and Coverage analyze state. Controlled Sync does not modify existing user audio files. Metadata Editor is the explicit write boundary and changes a file only after a user action.\n\nDiagnostic information excludes tokens, cookies, protected URLs and music-library contents. Normal MusicArk workflows must not silently delete user audio files.",
